{title: Blessed Is The One}
{subtitle: Psalms 65:5}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7] | [Eb] |
| [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Praise awaits in si[Abmaj7]lence O God
[Eb]In Zion the vow shall [Abmaj7]be met
[Cm7]You hear the prayer of all [Abmaj7]flesh
Iniquity [Bb]overwhelms the breast
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Cm7]You atone for our trans[Abmaj7]gressions
[Cm7]Your mercy covers our of[Abmaj7]fenses [Eb/G]
[Fm7]We dwell near you in your [Cm7]courts
Filled with [Abmaj7]goodness and sweet [Bb]sports
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Blessed is the one you [Eb/G][Ab]choose
[Cm]Brought near to dwell with [Ab]you
Filled with the good[Eb]ness of your [Ab]house
The holiness of [Bb]your temple [Eb][Ab]too
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Awesome deeds of right[Ab]eousness
[Eb]Answer us O our sal[Ab]vation
[Cm]Hope of all ends of the [Ab]earth
And the [Bb]farthest deep waters
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Blessed is the one you [Eb/G][Ab]choose
[Cm]Brought near to dwell with [Ab]you
Filled with the good[Eb]ness of your [Eb/G][Ab]house
The holiness of [Bb]your temple [Eb]too
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm]You set the [Ab]mountains [Eb]in [Bb]place
[Cm]Girded with [Ab]mighty pow[Eb][Bb]er
[Cm]You still [Ab]the roaring [Eb]of [Bb]the seas
And [Ab]the tumult of the [Bb]peoples
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Blessed is the one you [Ab]choose
[Cm]Brought near to dwell [Ab]with you
Filled with [Eb]the goodness [Ab]of your house
The holi[Bb]ness of your [Eb]temple too
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Blessed is the one [Eb/G]you [Ab]choose
[Cm]Brought near to dwell with [Ab]you [Eb]
{end_of_verse}
